---

## 🚀 Overview

This project presents an FPGA-accelerated image enhancement system using Residual Convolutional Neural Networks (Residual CNNs) with INT8 quantization and Vitis AI deployment.

The system is designed for:

- Real-time FPGA inference
- Edge AI deployment
- Low-light enhancement
- Noise reduction
- Blur restoration
- Efficient INT8 inference

---

## ✨ Features

- Residual CNN image enhancement
- FPGA-oriented deployment workflow
- INT8 Quantization-Aware Training
- Vitis AI integration
- DPU hardware acceleration
- Docker support
- PSNR / SSIM evaluation
- Hardware-software co-design workflow

---

## 🧠 System Architecture

```text
Dataset
   ↓
Residual CNN Training
   ↓
Quantization-Aware Training
   ↓
INT8 Optimization
   ↓
Vitis AI Compilation
   ↓
XModel Generation
   ↓
DPU Deployment
   ↓
FPGA Inference
   ↓
Enhanced Output
```

---

## ⚡ Performance

| Metric | CPU | FPGA |
|--------|------|------|
| Inference Speed | 0.85 – 1.3 FPS | 8.37 FPS |
| Precision | FP32 | INT8 |
| Speedup | 1× | 8–10× |
| Deployment | CPU | FPGA DPU |

